{"name":"Spiro Disco Ball","hex":"#0fc0fc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spiro","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A polycyclic compound or system that contains a single atom as the only common member of two rings."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of spironolactone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiro"},{"term":"disco","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of discotheque (“nightclub for dancing”).","A genre of dance music that was popular in the 1970s, characterized by elements of soul music with a strong Latin-American beat and often accompanied by pulsating lights."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dance disco-style dances.","To go to discotheques."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disco"},{"term":"ball","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A solid or hollow sphere, or roughly spherical mass.","A quantity of string, thread, etc., wound into a spherical shape."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form or wind into a ball.","To heat in a furnace and form into balls for rolling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ball"}],"entries":[{"title":"Disco ball","blocks":[{"text":"A disco ball is a roughly spherical object that reflects light directed at it in many directions, producing a complex display. Its surface consists of hundreds or thousands of facets, nearly all of approximately the same shape and size, and each has a mirrored surface. Usually, it is mounted well above the heads of the people present, suspended from a device that causes it to rotate steadily on a vertical axis, and illuminated by spotlights, so that stationary viewers experience beams of light flashing over them, and see myriad spots of light spinning around the walls of the room."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Mirrored_Disco_Ball_with_Light_and_Motor.jpg/330px-Mirrored_Disco_Ball_with_Light_and_Motor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disco_ball","wikidata":"Q1192656"},{"title":"Disco","blocks":[{"text":"Disco is a genre of dance music and a subculture that emerged in the late 1960s from the United States' urban nightlife scene. Its sound is typified by four-on-the-floor beats, syncopated basslines, string sections, brass and horns, electric pianos, synthesizers, and electric rhythm guitars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Disco_TGI_Bar_by_John_Vance.jpg/330px-Disco_TGI_Bar_by_John_Vance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disco","wikidata":"Q58339"},{"title":"Ball","blocks":[{"text":"A ball is a round object. Balls can have several uses. For example they are used in ball games, where the play of the game follows the state of the ball as it is hit, kicked or thrown by players. Balls can also be used for simpler activities, such as catch or juggling. Balls made from hard-wearing materials are used in engineering applications to provide very low friction bearings, known as ball bearings. Black-powder weapons use stone and metal balls as projectiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Many_balls.jpg/330px-Many_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball","wikidata":"Q18545"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/LouisianaFiveBandstand_%28restored_version%29.jpg/500px-LouisianaFiveBandstand_%28restored_version%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/LouisianaFiveBandstand_%28restored_version%29.jpg/500px-LouisianaFiveBandstand_%28restored_version%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A mirrored ball can be seen above the bandstand in this 1919 photo of the Louisiana Five jazz band.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALouisianaFiveBandstand_(restored_version).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Disco_Ball.JPG/500px-Disco_Ball.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Disco_Ball.JPG/1280px-Disco_Ball.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Disco_Ball.JPG/500px-Disco_Ball.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A disco ball and spotlight in the Fishbowl of Currier House","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADisco_Ball.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Disco_Santa.jpg/500px-Disco_Santa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Disco_Santa.jpg/1280px-Disco_Santa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Disco_Santa.jpg/500px-Disco_Santa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Disco Santa ornament typical of 2020s disco kitsch","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADisco_Santa.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/db/Blue_disco_quad_roller_skates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/db/Blue_disco_quad_roller_skates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Blue disco quad roller skates","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_disco_quad_roller_skates.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Dance_floor_2_by_harmon.jpg/500px-Dance_floor_2_by_harmon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Dance_floor_2_by_harmon.jpg/500px-Dance_floor_2_by_harmon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Major disco clubs had lighted dance floors, with the lights flashing to complement the beat.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADance_floor_2_by_harmon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg/500px-ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg/1280px-ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg/500px-ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The reflective light disco ball was a fixture on the ceilings of many discothèques.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG/500px-04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG/1280px-04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG/500px-04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Disco dancers typically wore loose slacks for men and flowing dresses for women, which enabled ease of movement on the dance floor.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Fotothek_df_n-15_0000413_Disko.jpg/500px-Fotothek_df_n-15_0000413_Disko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Fotothek_df_n-15_0000413_Disko.jpg/500px-Fotothek_df_n-15_0000413_Disko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dancers at an East German discothèque in 1977. Due to the constant scarcity of consumer goods in the then socialist part of Germany, particularly more exotic fashion items like disco wear, people often sewed them themselves.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFotothek_df_n-15_0000413_Disko.jpg"}],"sounds":{"spiro":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d1/En-au-spiro.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d1/En-au-spiro.ogg/En-au-spiro.ogg.mp3"}],"disco":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-disco.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-disco.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-disco.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-disco.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-disco.wav.ogg"}],"ball":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a8/En-us-ball.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg